BETA TEST Amiga-native subversion 1.1.4 software for the Amiga
==============================================================

1. What is this beta test update about?

This archive contains the first update to the Amiga-native subversion 1.1.4
port in almost 10 years. The need for the update arose with the changes
which happened to the technology and infrastructure which the subversion
software uses to securely access repositories. The protocols and data that
underpins this technology have changed greatly in the past 10 years.

The changes made insure that you will be able to access subversion
repositories via https:// that use modern security certificates. Previous
versions, such as version 1.9 of this subversion port, would be unable to do
so consistently because they were unable to verify the complete certificate
chain, i.e. you would likely end up having to confirm to the subversion
commands that you were willing to accept a security certificate which could
not be verified as being secure.

Due to the nature of the changes, which affect the whole operation of the
programs in this package, beta testing it before it is released for general
use seems to be prudent.

The beta test starts with version 1.10 of this subversion port. It includes
the following shell commands:

