2. What has changed and how does this impact you?

This version has been modified to use the (currently) most recent AmiSSL 4.4
software.

While the source code of this Amiga-native subversion software is now more
than 10 years old, it was possible to update it. Thanks to Costel Mincea, who
researched and implemented the necessary changes, the AmiSSL V4 support will
allow you to access subversion repositories secured with modern certificates.

This extends the usefulness of this subversion port a little further until a
new replacement port based upon the current subversion release can be made.

One drawback of this modernized subversion port is in that the subversion
commands use the possibly oldest data exchange protocol when "talking" to
a subversion server. You would be able to access modern subversion servers
with it, but this protocol is too old for modern git servers, for example.


3. Requirements

You need to install AmiSSL V4 software in order to use this beta test
version, as otherwise none of the subversion commands will work at all.

You can find the AmiSSL V4 software here:

   https://github.com/jens-maus/amissl/

The individual archives you might want to download can be found here:

   https://github.com/jens-maus/amissl/releases/download/4.4/AmiSSL-4.4.lha
   https://github.com/jens-maus/amissl/releases/download/4.4/AmiSSL-4.4.readme
   https://github.com/jens-maus/amissl/releases/download/4.4/AmiSSL-4.4.lha.sha256

Two sets of commands are provided in this archive. One set was built for the
AmigaOS 3.x operating system and requires an Amiga equipped with an 68020 CPU
(or better). The other set was built for Amiga computers running AmigaOS 4.x.

As with previous versions of these tools, you need a working TCP/IP stack
and enough free memory to both load the respective shell commands (such as
the "svn" command) and the AmiSSL libraries.

Please consult the "AMIGA.README" file supplied with this archive for more
detailed requirement information.


